course: dictionary
lesson: 8964
title: Words from the real world: simulator
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A simulator is a machine or computer program that copies real conditions, so you can practise or test something safely. «Pilots learn real skills in simulators» means pilots train in a copy of a plane before they fly a real one. The word itself is a clue: a simulator copies something.
explain: Use the context to check. «Think of a pilot in a flight simulator: the cockpit is a model, but the skill is real.» A model is a copy, so the cockpit in the simulator copies a real one, but the skill it teaches is real. Swap in your meaning: "pilots train in a copy of a plane" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: A simulator can also be a computer game that copies a real activity, such as a farm simulator or a driving simulator. Phrases like «flight simulator», «driving simulator» and «train on a simulator» are useful clues. The plural is simulators.
fact: A simulator copies real conditions so people can practise safely.
fact: «Simulator» is a noun, and its plural is simulators.
fact: A simulation is a model of something real, built to explore or learn.
fact: Pilots and astronauts train on simulators before they fly real planes or spacecraft.
fact: Some simulators are computer games, such as a farm simulator or a cooking simulator.
exercise: «Pilots learn real skills in simulators.» Where do pilots practise safely? | On a crowded airport runway | In a school playground | *In a simulator | At the seaside
exercise: «Think of a pilot in a flight simulator: the cockpit is a model.» What does model mean here? | A pilot's helmet | A type of aeroplane | *A copy of something real
exercise: Which of these is a simulator game that copies a real activity? | *A farm simulator | A farmer's market | A farm animal | A tractor race
test: «A flight simulator teaches pilots without crashing real planes.» What is the main benefit? | They never need to learn | *They practise safely | They get a free plane | They fly faster
test: Which word is the plural of simulator? | *simulators | simulate | simulator's | simulatering
exam: Which sentence uses simulator correctly? | The simulator flew over the sea with its wings | Yesterday we simulatored the cake | *The pilot trained on a flight simulator before flying a real plane | Simulator is a colour of the sky
